rent investigators I should  comment at this point that heavy light  has actually been FDA approved in Europe  for over a year and has been widely used  especially by the French group and so I  think we're pretty confident about the  normal ranges that we have clearly the  FDA bought into it which is always  important  thank you the next question is from  Zhang Xiao a clinical chemistry fellow  from Houston Methodist Hospital two  questions the first question could this  heavy light as they diagnose heavy chain  disease the second one is he let such he  wants to know if he can have your slides  and this will be posted online for a  while so I can answer that one so it's  actually an interesting question and I  would say right now the answer is as  best we understand it probably would not  work very well on heavy chain disease  and that is because the reagent  recognizes combination epitopes of heavy  and light chains this is not every agent  that recognizes igg it recognizes i GG  kappa specifically so it recognizes  conformational epitopes form between the  pairing of g kappa and g lambda thank  you the next question are there any  efforts at this time to incorporate the  heavy light assay into the international  guidelines for myeloma response so  that's a great question the answer is  yeah we're absolutely working on it  binding site has a history of working  very closely with the international  myeloma working group many of the  members of this group are  enthusiastically looking at heavy light  in clinical studies right now that many  of which we hope will be published this  year and I know that they are now  looking at whether or not this should be  incorporated into a revision of the  guidelines for diagnosing and monitoring  plasma cell disclosures  our next question could heavyweight  replace ife i'm going to say the answer  to that really is yes and no and and the  way i would suggest it that it be used  is you probably aren't going to want to  run heavy l